      "anchor": {
        "mission_intent": "Subject: Review and Update of Incident Evidence Retention Policy\n\nTeam, we need to conduct a thorough review of our current evidence retention procedures for incident response artifacts. Legal has flagged that we don't have clear guidance reconciling our general data retention windows with the needs of potential prosecution cases, where evidence may need to be preserved for extended and sometimes unpredictable periods. Please draft an updated evidence retention policy section that addresses the following: first, establish a baseline retention period for incident handling records that aligns with federal records scheduling requirements; second, define an exception process for cases where law enforcement involvement or pending litigation requires indefinite preservation of forensic images, disk captures, and related artifacts, even when those artifacts contain data types that would normally age out under our standard retention schedules such as the 180-day window for email; and third, include cost-management provisions for storing original hardware like hard drives and compromised systems that must be retained as evidence, including criteria for when forensic copies can substitute for physical media. Route the draft through Legal and the CISO's office for review by end of next quarter. We need this tightened up before our next audit cycle.",
